{"id":"rhel-07","n":7,"subject":"rhel","title":"Controlling Access to Files","display":"Chapter 7: Controlling Access to Files","sourceFile":"RHEL_SysAdmin_I_Ch07_Study.docx","sourceSha256":"bffb63ed213026f418addcff89be0ad36b015f49babf719b05b0c9e2ffa90870","blocks":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Chapter 7","b":true,"c":"#1F4E79"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Controlling Access to Files","b":true,"c":"#1F4E79"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux System Administration I | Study","c":"#595959"}]},{"k":"h","lvl":1,"runs":[{"t":"Chapter goal"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"This chapter shows you how Linux decides who may read, change or run a file. You learn to read permissions, change them, and change who owns a file. You also learn the special permissions and the default permissions that new files get."}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Topics in book order:"}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"Interpreting Linux File System Permissions"}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"Managing File System Permissions from the Command Line"}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"Managing Default Permissions and File Access"}]},{"k":"h","lvl":1,"runs":[{"t":"Interpreting Linux File System Permissions"}]},{"k":"h","lvl":2,"runs":[{"t":"1.1 The three categories: user, group, and other"}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#DDEBF7","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Main idea: ","b":true,"c":"#1F4E79"},{"t":"Every file has permissions for three categories of people: the owning user, the owning group, and everyone else.","c":"#000000"}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Simple explanation:","b":true},{"t":" Think of a house. The owner has one set of rules, family members (the group) have another, and visitors (other) have a third. A file is owned by one user, normally its creator. It is also owned by one group, usually the creator's primary group, but this can change. "},{"t":"Other","b":true},{"t":" means anyone who is neither the owner nor in the owning group. The most specific rule wins: user permissions override group permissions, and group permissions override other."}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Example:","b":true}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"The book's sample: "},{"t":"joshua"},{"t":" is in groups "},{"t":"joshua"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"web"},{"t":", and "},{"t":"allison"},{"t":" is in "},{"t":"allison"},{"t":", "},{"t":"wheel"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"web"},{"t":". For them to work together, the files should belong to group "},{"t":"web"},{"t":", with group permissions that allow the access they need."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#F2F2F2","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"(no command: this is how to plan sharing)"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"owner: joshua   group: web   other: everyone else"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"What each part means:","b":true}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"User: the one owner of the file."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"Group: the one owning group; every member shares its permissions."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"Other: all remaining users."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#E2EFDA","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Remember: ","b":true,"c":"#375623"},{"t":"The most specific category wins: user, then group, then other.","c":"#375623"}],"fill":"#E2EFDA"}]},{"k":"h","lvl":2,"runs":[{"t":"1.2 Read, write, and execute"}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#DDEBF7","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Main idea: ","b":true,"c":"#1F4E79"},{"t":"Three permissions exist, and they mean different things for files and for directories.","c":"#000000"}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Simple explanation:","b":true},{"t":" For a file, "},{"t":"read","b":true},{"t":" ("},{"t":"r"},{"t":") lets you view the contents, "},{"t":"write","b":true},{"t":" ("},{"t":"w"},{"t":") lets you change them, and "},{"t":"execute","b":true},{"t":" ("},{"t":"x"},{"t":") lets you run the file as a command. For a directory, "},{"t":"r"},{"t":" lets you list the file names, "},{"t":"w"},{"t":" lets you create or delete files inside, and "},{"t":"x"},{"t":" lets you enter it and reach its contents. A good comparison is a room: "},{"t":"x"},{"t":" is the key to the door, and "},{"t":"r"},{"t":" is the window that lets you see what is inside. Users normally get both "},{"t":"r"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"x"},{"t":" on a directory. With only "},{"t":"r"},{"t":" you can see names but nothing else. With only "},{"t":"x"},{"t":" you cannot list names, but you can open a file if you already know its exact name. Anyone with "},{"t":"w"},{"t":" on a directory can delete any file in it, whatever the file's own permissions (the sticky bit changes this; see 3.1)."}]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"runs":[{"t":"Permission","b":true}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"},{"runs":[{"t":"On a file","b":true}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"},{"runs":[{"t":"On a directory","b":true}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"}],[{"runs":[{"t":"r"},{"t":" read"}]},{"runs":[{"t":"Read the contents"}]},{"runs":[{"t":"List the file names"}]}],[{"runs":[{"t":"w"},{"t":" write"}]},{"runs":[{"t":"Change the contents"}]},{"runs":[{"t":"Create or delete files in it"}]}],[{"runs":[{"t":"x"},{"t":" execute"}]},{"runs":[{"t":"Run it as a command"}]},{"runs":[{"t":"Enter it and reach its files, if their permissions allow"}]}]],"headRow":true},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Tip: Linux permissions differ from Windows NTFS. They apply only to the item they are set on and are not inherited by items inside a directory, though a strict directory can block access to its contents. Directory "},{"t":"r"},{"t":" is like \"List folder contents\" and directory "},{"t":"w"},{"t":" is like \"Modify\". With "},{"t":"w"},{"t":" plus the sticky bit, only the owner can delete a file, which is close to Windows Write. Root has the equivalent of Full Control, but SELinux (taught in a later course) may still limit it."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#E2EFDA","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Remember: ","b":true,"c":"#375623"},{"t":"Directory ","c":"#375623"},{"t":"x","c":"#375623"},{"t":" lets you in; directory ","c":"#375623"},{"t":"w","c":"#375623"},{"t":" lets you create and delete.","c":"#375623"}],"fill":"#E2EFDA"}]},{"k":"h","lvl":2,"runs":[{"t":"1.3 Viewing permissions and ownership with ls -l"}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#DDEBF7","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Main idea: ","b":true,"c":"#1F4E79"},{"t":"ls -l","c":"#000000"},{"t":" shows the file type, the three permission sets, and the owner and group.","c":"#000000"}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Simple explanation:","b":true},{"t":" Read the line from left to right like a label on a box. The first character is the type: "},{"t":"-"},{"t":" regular file, "},{"t":"d"},{"t":" directory, "},{"t":"l"},{"t":" soft link; "},{"t":"b"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"c"},{"t":" are devices, and "},{"t":"p"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"s"},{"t":" are other special files. The next nine characters are three sets of three: user, group, other. A letter means \"allowed\" and "},{"t":"-"},{"t":" means \"not allowed\". After the link count come the owning user, then the owning group. The "},{"t":"-d"},{"t":" option lists a directory itself, not its contents."}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Example:","b":true}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Run on "},{"t":"servera"},{"t":". It only reads. A dot after the permissions is a security label you can ignore for now."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#F2F2F2","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ ls -l test"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ ls -ld /home"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Output:","b":true}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"-rw-rw-r--. 1 student student 0 Feb  8 17:36 test"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"drwxr-xr-x. 5 root root 4096 Jan 31 22:00 /home"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"What each part means:","b":true}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"-rw-rw-r--"},{"t":": file; user "},{"t":"rw-"},{"t":", group "},{"t":"rw-"},{"t":", other "},{"t":"r--"},{"t":"."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"student student"},{"t":": owner and owning group."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"So user "},{"t":"student"},{"t":" can read and write "},{"t":"test"},{"t":" but not run it. Other users can only read it."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#E2EFDA","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Remember: ","b":true,"c":"#375623"},{"t":"Type, then user, group and other triplets, then owner and group names.","c":"#375623"}],"fill":"#E2EFDA"}]},{"k":"h","lvl":2,"runs":[{"t":"1.4 Working out who can do what"}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#DDEBF7","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Main idea: ","b":true,"c":"#1F4E79"},{"t":"To find a user's access, check whether they are the owner, then in the group, then fall back to other.","c":"#000000"}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Simple explanation:","b":true},{"t":" Ask three questions in order: Is this user the owner? If not, are they in the owning group? If not, the other set applies. Stop at the first yes. In the book's example, "},{"t":"operator1"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"database1"},{"t":" are in group "},{"t":"consultant1"},{"t":". The user "},{"t":"database2"},{"t":" is in neither, so "},{"t":"other"},{"t":" applies to that user."}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Example:","b":true}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Run on "},{"t":"servera"},{"t":". It only reads. "},{"t":"ls -la"},{"t":" also shows hidden files, including "},{"t":"."},{"t":" (this directory) and "},{"t":".."},{"t":" (its parent)."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#F2F2F2","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[database1@host dir]$ ls -la"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Output:","b":true}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"drwxrwxr-x.  2 database1 consultant1  4096 Apr  4 10:23 ."}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"-rw-rw-r--.  1 operator1 operator1    1024 Apr  4 11:02 lfile1"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"-rw-r--rw-.  1 operator1 consultant1  3144 Apr  4 11:02 lfile2"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"-rw-rw-r--.  1 database1 consultant1 10234 Apr  4 10:14 rfile1"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"-rw-r-----.  1 database1 consultant1  2048 Apr  4 10:18 rfile2"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"What each part means:","b":true}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"operator1"},{"t":" can change "},{"t":"rfile1"},{"t":": group "},{"t":"consultant1"},{"t":" has read and write."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"database2"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"contractor1"},{"t":" cannot read "},{"t":"rfile2"},{"t":": other has no permissions."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"database1"},{"t":" can read but not change "},{"t":"lfile2"},{"t":": group "},{"t":"consultant1"},{"t":" has only read, and the group set beats other (which has write)."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"database1"},{"t":" can delete "},{"t":"lfile1"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"lfile2"},{"t":": it has write on the directory "},{"t":"."},{"t":"."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#E2EFDA","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Remember: ","b":true,"c":"#375623"},{"t":"Owner first, then group, then other; deleting depends on the directory's ","c":"#375623"},{"t":"w","c":"#375623"},{"t":".","c":"#375623"}],"fill":"#E2EFDA"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Where to read more:","b":true},{"t":" "},{"t":"ls(1)"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"info coreutils"},{"t":" section 13 (Changing file attributes)."}]},{"k":"h","lvl":1,"runs":[{"t":"Managing File System Permissions from the Command Line"}]},{"k":"h","lvl":2,"runs":[{"t":"2.1 Changing permissions with the symbolic method"}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#DDEBF7","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Main idea: ","b":true,"c":"#1F4E79"},{"t":"chmod","c":"#000000"},{"t":" changes permissions, and the symbolic method uses letters: who, what, which.","c":"#000000"}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Simple explanation:","b":true},{"t":" The name "},{"t":"chmod"},{"t":" means \"change mode\" (permissions are also called the mode). Think of a set of light switches: you can flip one without touching the rest. The format is "},{"t":"chmod WhoWhatWhich file"},{"t":". "},{"t":"Who","b":true},{"t":" is "},{"t":"u"},{"t":" (user), "},{"t":"g"},{"t":" (group), "},{"t":"o"},{"t":" (other) or "},{"t":"a"},{"t":" (all). "},{"t":"What","b":true},{"t":" is "},{"t":"+"},{"t":" (add), "},{"t":"-"},{"t":" (remove) or "},{"t":"="},{"t":" (set exactly). "},{"t":"Which","b":true},{"t":" is "},{"t":"r"},{"t":", "},{"t":"w"},{"t":" or "},{"t":"x"},{"t":". A capital "},{"t":"X"},{"t":" adds execute only to directories, or to files that already have execute for someone."}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Example:","b":true}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Run on "},{"t":"servera"},{"t":" as the file's owner. Check with "},{"t":"ls -l"},{"t":". Undo with the opposite command."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#F2F2F2","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ ls -l file1"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ chmod go-rw file1"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ ls -l file1"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ chmod a+x file2"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Output:","b":true}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"-rw-rw-r--. 1 user user 0 Feb 8 17:36 file1"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"-rw-------. 1 user user 0 Feb 8 17:36 file1"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"What each part means:","b":true}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"go-rw"},{"t":" removes read and write from group and other."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"a+x"},{"t":" adds execute for everyone."}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Tip: "},{"t":"chmod -R"},{"t":" changes a whole directory tree. With "},{"t":"-R"},{"t":", the symbolic "},{"t":"X"},{"t":" is handy: it sets execute on directories so their contents stay reachable, without changing most files. Be careful, though, because a file that already has any execute bit also gets it. For example, "},{"t":"chmod -R g+rwX demodir"},{"t":" (run as root in "},{"t":"/opt"},{"t":") sets group read and write on everything in "},{"t":"demodir"},{"t":", and group execute only on directories and files that already have execute."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#E2EFDA","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Remember: ","b":true,"c":"#375623"},{"t":"Pick who, pick ","c":"#375623"},{"t":"+","c":"#375623"},{"t":", ","c":"#375623"},{"t":"-","c":"#375623"},{"t":" or ","c":"#375623"},{"t":"=","c":"#375623"},{"t":", pick which: ","c":"#375623"},{"t":"chmod go-rw file","c":"#375623"},{"t":".","c":"#375623"}],"fill":"#E2EFDA"}]},{"k":"h","lvl":2,"runs":[{"t":"2.2 Changing permissions with the numeric method"}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#DDEBF7","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Main idea: ","b":true,"c":"#1F4E79"},{"t":"The numeric method writes permissions as three digits, one each for user, group and other.","c":"#000000"}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Simple explanation:","b":true},{"t":" Each permission has a value: read is 4, write is 2, execute is 1. Add the values you want for each category. It is like a shopping total: "},{"t":"rwx"},{"t":" is 4+2+1=7, "},{"t":"r-x"},{"t":" is 4+0+1=5, and "},{"t":"---"},{"t":" is 0. So "},{"t":"-rwxr-x---"},{"t":" is "},{"t":"750"},{"t":". It also works backward: "},{"t":"640"},{"t":" means "},{"t":"rw-"},{"t":" for user (4+2), "},{"t":"r--"},{"t":" for group (4), and "},{"t":"---"},{"t":" for other (0), which is "},{"t":"-rw-r-----"},{"t":". Administrators like it because it is short. A 4th digit in front is used for special permissions (see 3.2)."}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Example:","b":true}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Run on "},{"t":"servera"},{"t":" as the owner. Check with "},{"t":"ls -l"},{"t":". Undo by setting the old number."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#F2F2F2","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ chmod 644 samplefile"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ chmod 750 sampledir"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ ls -ld sampledir"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Output:","b":true}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"drwxr-x---. 2 user user 6 Feb 8 17:40 sampledir"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"What each part means:","b":true}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"644"},{"t":": user "},{"t":"rw-"},{"t":", group "},{"t":"r--"},{"t":", other "},{"t":"r--"},{"t":"."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"750"},{"t":": user "},{"t":"rwx"},{"t":", group "},{"t":"r-x"},{"t":", other nothing."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#E2EFDA","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Remember: ","b":true,"c":"#375623"},{"t":"4 = read, 2 = write, 1 = execute; add them for each category.","c":"#375623"}],"fill":"#E2EFDA"}]},{"k":"h","lvl":2,"runs":[{"t":"2.3 Changing ownership with chown and chgrp"}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#DDEBF7","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Main idea: ","b":true,"c":"#1F4E79"},{"t":"chown","c":"#000000"},{"t":" changes who owns a file, and ","c":"#000000"},{"t":"chgrp","c":"#000000"},{"t":" changes only the owning group.","c":"#000000"}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Simple explanation:","b":true},{"t":" New files belong to the user who creates them and to that user's primary group. Only root can change the owning user. The owner can change the group, but only to a group the owner belongs to. Root can use any group. Use "},{"t":"chown owner file"},{"t":" for the user, "},{"t":"chown :group file"},{"t":" for the group, and "},{"t":"chown owner:group file"},{"t":" for both. "},{"t":"-R"},{"t":" works on a whole tree. "},{"t":"chgrp"},{"t":" does the same job for groups but needs no colon."}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Example:","b":true}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Run on "},{"t":"servera"},{"t":" as root. Check with "},{"t":"ls -l"},{"t":". Undo by running "},{"t":"chown"},{"t":" with the old names."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#F2F2F2","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[root@host ~]# chown student test_file"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[root@host ~]# chown -R student test_dir"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[root@host ~]# chown :admins test_dir"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[root@host ~]# chown visitor:guests test_dir"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[root@host ~]# chgrp guests test_dir"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Output:","b":true}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"(no output; `ls -l` shows the new owner and group names)"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"What each part means:","b":true}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"student"},{"t":" alone sets the owner."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":":admins"},{"t":" sets only the group."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"visitor:guests"},{"t":" sets both."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"-R"},{"t":" applies it to everything inside."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#FFF2CC","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Important: ","b":true,"c":"#7F6000"},{"t":"You may see ","c":"#7F6000"},{"t":"chown owner.group file","c":"#7F6000"},{"t":", with a period. Do not use it. A period is a valid character in a user name, but a colon is not. If the user ","c":"#7F6000"},{"t":"enoch.root","c":"#7F6000"},{"t":", the user ","c":"#7F6000"},{"t":"enoch","c":"#7F6000"},{"t":" and the group ","c":"#7F6000"},{"t":"root","c":"#7F6000"},{"t":" all exist, ","c":"#7F6000"},{"t":"chown enoch.root file","c":"#7F6000"},{"t":" makes ","c":"#7F6000"},{"t":"enoch.root","c":"#7F6000"},{"t":" the owner, which may not be what you meant. Always use the colon.","c":"#7F6000"}],"fill":"#FFF2CC"}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#E2EFDA","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Remember: ","b":true,"c":"#375623"},{"t":"Use ","c":"#375623"},{"t":"chown owner:group file","c":"#375623"},{"t":" with a colon; only root changes the owner.","c":"#375623"}],"fill":"#E2EFDA"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Where to read more:","b":true},{"t":" "},{"t":"ls(1)"},{"t":", "},{"t":"chmod(1)"},{"t":", "},{"t":"chown(1)"},{"t":", "},{"t":"chgrp(1)"},{"t":"."}]},{"k":"h","lvl":1,"runs":[{"t":"Managing Default Permissions and File Access"}]},{"k":"h","lvl":2,"runs":[{"t":"3.1 Special permissions"}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#DDEBF7","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Main idea: ","b":true,"c":"#1F4E79"},{"t":"Special permissions are a fourth type that adds extra access features: setuid, setgid and the sticky bit.","c":"#000000"}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Simple explanation:","b":true},{"t":" Think of three special badges. "},{"t":"setuid","b":true},{"t":" ("},{"t":"u+s"},{"t":") on a program makes it run as the file's owner, not as the person who ran it. The "},{"t":"passwd"},{"t":" command uses this. "},{"t":"setgid","b":true},{"t":" ("},{"t":"g+s"},{"t":") on a program runs it as the owning group. On a directory it makes new files take the directory's group, which is handy for shared folders. The "},{"t":"sticky bit","b":true},{"t":" ("},{"t":"o+t"},{"t":") on a directory means users can delete only their own files there. "},{"t":"/tmp"},{"t":" uses it."}]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"runs":[{"t":"Special","b":true}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"},{"runs":[{"t":"On files","b":true}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"},{"runs":[{"t":"On directories","b":true}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"}],[{"runs":[{"t":"u+s"},{"t":" (setuid)"}]},{"runs":[{"t":"Runs as the user who owns the file"}]},{"runs":[{"t":"No effect"}]}],[{"runs":[{"t":"g+s"},{"t":" (setgid)"}]},{"runs":[{"t":"Runs as the group that owns the file"}]},{"runs":[{"t":"New files get the directory's group"}]}],[{"runs":[{"t":"o+t"},{"t":" (sticky)"}]},{"runs":[{"t":"No effect"}]},{"runs":[{"t":"Users can delete only their own files"}]}]],"headRow":true},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Example:","b":true}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Run on "},{"t":"servera"},{"t":". It only reads."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#F2F2F2","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ ls -l /usr/bin/passwd"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ ls -ld /run/log/journal"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ ls -ld /tmp"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Output:","b":true}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"-rwsr-xr-x. 1 root root 35504 Jul 16  2010 /usr/bin/passwd"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"drwxr-sr-x. 3 root systemd-journal 60 May 18 09:15 /run/log/journal"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"drwxrwxrwt. 39 root root 4096 Feb  8 20:52 /tmp"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"What each part means:","b":true}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"A lowercase "},{"t":"s"},{"t":" replaces "},{"t":"x"},{"t":" for setuid (user set) or setgid (group set). A lowercase "},{"t":"t"},{"t":" replaces "},{"t":"x"},{"t":" in the other set."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"A capital "},{"t":"S"},{"t":" or "},{"t":"T"},{"t":" means the matching "},{"t":"x"},{"t":" is missing."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"The book also shows "},{"t":"locate"},{"t":" as a setgid program, "},{"t":"-rwx--s--x"},{"t":"."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#E2EFDA","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Remember: ","b":true,"c":"#375623"},{"t":"s","c":"#375623"},{"t":" in user or group, ","c":"#375623"},{"t":"t","c":"#375623"},{"t":" in other: look at the ","c":"#375623"},{"t":"x","c":"#375623"},{"t":" position.","c":"#375623"}],"fill":"#E2EFDA"}]},{"k":"h","lvl":2,"runs":[{"t":"3.2 Setting special permissions"}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#DDEBF7","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Main idea: ","b":true,"c":"#1F4E79"},{"t":"You set special permissions with ","c":"#000000"},{"t":"chmod","c":"#000000"},{"t":", in symbolic form or with a fourth digit in front.","c":"#000000"}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Simple explanation:","b":true},{"t":" Symbolically, use "},{"t":"u+s"},{"t":" for setuid, "},{"t":"g+s"},{"t":" for setgid and "},{"t":"o+t"},{"t":" for sticky. Numerically, put a digit in front of the usual three: 4 for setuid, 2 for setgid, 1 for sticky. They add up the same way as read, write and execute. So "},{"t":"2770"},{"t":" means setgid plus "},{"t":"rwx"},{"t":" for user and group, and nothing for other."}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Example:","b":true}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Run on "},{"t":"servera"},{"t":" as root. Check with "},{"t":"ls -ld directory"},{"t":". Undo with "},{"t":"chmod g-s directory"},{"t":"."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#F2F2F2","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[root@host ~]# chmod g+s directory"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[root@host ~]# chmod 2770 directory"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[root@host ~]# ls -ld directory"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Output:","b":true}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"drwxrws---. 2 root consultants 6 Feb 1 13:21 directory"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"What each part means:","b":true}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"g+s"},{"t":" adds setgid to the group set."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"2770"},{"t":": 2 = setgid, 7 = user "},{"t":"rwx"},{"t":", 7 = group "},{"t":"rwx"},{"t":", 0 = other nothing."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#E2EFDA","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Remember: ","b":true,"c":"#375623"},{"t":"Digits 4, 2, 1 in front mean setuid, setgid and sticky.","c":"#375623"}],"fill":"#E2EFDA"}]},{"k":"h","lvl":2,"runs":[{"t":"3.3 Default permissions and the umask"}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#DDEBF7","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Main idea: ","b":true,"c":"#1F4E79"},{"t":"New files and directories start with full permissions, and the umask removes some of them.","c":"#000000"}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Simple explanation:","b":true},{"t":" A new directory starts at "},{"t":"0777"},{"t":" ("},{"t":"drwxrwxrwx"},{"t":"). A new regular file starts at "},{"t":"0666"},{"t":" ("},{"t":"-rw-rw-rw-"},{"t":"), because you must add execute yourself. This makes it harder for an attacker to create a file and run it at once. The "},{"t":"umask","b":true},{"t":" is a mask: each bit that is set removes that permission from new files. A umask of "},{"t":"0002"},{"t":" removes write for other. A umask of "},{"t":"0077"},{"t":" removes everything for group and other. Run "},{"t":"umask"},{"t":" with no argument to see it. Run "},{"t":"umask 027"},{"t":" to change it for the current shell only."}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Example:","b":true}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Run on "},{"t":"servera"},{"t":" as a normal user. It creates test files and folders; remove them with "},{"t":"rm"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"rmdir"},{"t":"."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#F2F2F2","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ umask"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ touch default.txt"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ ls -l default.txt"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ umask 027"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ touch two-seven.txt"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"[user@host ~]$ ls -l two-seven.txt"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Output:","b":true}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"0002"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"-rw-rw-r--. 1 user user 0 May 9 01:54 default.txt"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"-rw-r-----. 1 user user 0 May 9 01:55 two-seven.txt"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"What each part means:","b":true}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"touch name"},{"t":" makes an empty file."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"With "},{"t":"0002"},{"t":" the file gets "},{"t":"rw-rw-r--"},{"t":"."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"With "},{"t":"027"},{"t":", group loses write, and other loses everything: "},{"t":"rw-r-----"},{"t":"."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"With "},{"t":"umask 007"},{"t":", files get "},{"t":"rw-rw----"},{"t":" and folders get "},{"t":"rwxrwx---"},{"t":"."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#E2EFDA","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Remember: ","b":true,"c":"#375623"},{"t":"The umask subtracts from 0666 for files and 0777 for directories.","c":"#375623"}],"fill":"#E2EFDA"}]},{"k":"h","lvl":2,"runs":[{"t":"3.4 Making umask changes permanent"}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#DDEBF7","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Main idea: ","b":true,"c":"#1F4E79"},{"t":"A global umask is set by shell startup scripts, and root can override it with a file in ","c":"#000000"},{"t":"/etc/profile.d","c":"#000000"},{"t":".","c":"#000000"}],"fill":"#DDEBF7"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Simple explanation:","b":true},{"t":" The default is set in "},{"t":"/etc/profile"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"/etc/bashrc"},{"t":", and each user can override it in "},{"t":".bash_profile"},{"t":" and "},{"t":".bashrc"},{"t":" in their home folder. By default, if your UID is 200 or more and your user name matches your primary group name, you get "},{"t":"002"},{"t":". Otherwise you get "},{"t":"022"},{"t":". As root, create "},{"t":"/etc/profile.d/local-umask.sh"},{"t":" to change this. The change shows only after you log out and in again; until then the old umask stays."}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Example:","b":true}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Run on "},{"t":"servera"},{"t":" as root. It creates a new file. Undo by deleting "},{"t":"/etc/profile.d/local-umask.sh"},{"t":"."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#F2F2F2","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"# /etc/profile.d/local-umask.sh"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"# Overrides default umask configuration"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"if [ $UID -gt 199 ] && [ \"`id -gn`\" = \"`id -un`\" ]; then"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"     umask 007"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"else"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"     umask 022"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"fi"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Output:","b":true}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"(no output; after you log in again, run umask to check)"}],"fill":"#F2F2F2"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"What each part means:","b":true}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"#"},{"t":" starts a comment."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"$UID"},{"t":" is your user number; "},{"t":"id -gn"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"id -un"},{"t":" print your group name and user name."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"If the UID is above 199 and the names match, umask is 007. Otherwise it is 022."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"To use 022 for everyone, make the file with only the comment line and "},{"t":"umask 022"},{"t":"."}]},{"k":"box","fill":"#E2EFDA","paras":[{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Remember: ","b":true,"c":"#375623"},{"t":"Put a global umask in ","c":"#375623"},{"t":"/etc/profile.d/local-umask.sh","c":"#375623"},{"t":", then log in again.","c":"#375623"}],"fill":"#E2EFDA"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Where to read more:","b":true},{"t":" "},{"t":"bash(1)"},{"t":", "},{"t":"ls(1)"},{"t":", "},{"t":"chmod(1)"},{"t":", "},{"t":"umask(1)"},{"t":"."}]},{"k":"h","lvl":1,"runs":[{"t":"Connecting the chapter"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Scenario:","b":true},{"t":" On "},{"t":"servera"},{"t":", you make a shared folder for the "},{"t":"consultants"},{"t":" group. As root, you run "},{"t":"chown :consultants /home/consultants"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"chmod 2770 /home/consultants"},{"t":". Now group members can create and delete files there, other users have no access, and new files take the group "},{"t":"consultants"},{"t":"."}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"Big picture:","b":true},{"t":" 1) Read permissions with "},{"t":"ls -l"},{"t":". 2) Change them with "},{"t":"chmod"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"chown"},{"t":". 3) Use setgid and the umask so new files get the right access."}]},{"k":"h","lvl":1,"runs":[{"t":"Skipped for clarity"}]},{"k":"p","runs":[{"t":"These details were left out on purpose. Look them up in the book by title."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"Interpreting Linux File System Permissions: the Quiz at the end of that section, and Figure 7.1."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"Guided Exercises for the command line and for default permissions (the "},{"t":"lab perms-..."},{"t":" steps and their two short NOTE boxes about the group owner and about exiting all shells)."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"Lab: Controlling Access to Files."}]},{"k":"li","runs":[{"t":"Managing Default Permissions and File Access: in the umask example, the book runs "},{"t":"touch default"},{"t":" but then lists "},{"t":"default.txt"},{"t":". This file uses "},{"t":"default.txt"},{"t":" both times."}]}],"h":17,"p":54,"li":38,"box":33,"tbl":2,"tableCells":24,"runs":710,"words":2898,"boxes":33,"shadedParas":87,"colourPairs":["#000000|#DDEBF7","#1F4E79|#DDEBF7","#1F4E79|page","#375623|#E2EFDA","#595959|page","#7F6000|#FFF2CC"]}
